.TH GCODE-LS 1 "2026-08-20" "gcode-language-server 0.0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gcode-ls \- Language Server Protocol implementation for G-code files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gcode-ls
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gcode-ls
runs a Language Server Protocol server for G-code files.
It reads JSON-RPC messages from standard input and writes responses to standard
output.
.PP
The server provides parsing, validation, completion, hover, and document symbol
features for G-code editors. It uses the Prusa flavor by default and supports
other G-code dialects through flavor files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-flavor " FLAVOR"
Select the G-code flavor to use, such as
.BR prusa ,
.BR marlin , or
.BR klipper .
.TP
.BI \-\-flavor-dir " DIRECTORY"
Search
.I DIRECTORY
for custom flavor TOML files.
.TP
.BI \-\-log-level " LEVEL"
Set the log level. Accepted values are
.BR trace ,
.BR debug ,
.BR info ,
.BR warn , and
.BR error .
The default is
.BR info .
.TP
.BR \-h , \-\-help
Print help information.
.TP
.BR \-V , \-\-version
Print version information.
.SH FLAVOR SELECTION
The built-in Prusa flavor is used unless another flavor is selected with
.BR \-\-flavor .
The server writes the embedded Prusa flavor to
.I ~/.gcode-ls/flavors/prusa.gcode-flavor.toml
when that file does not already exist.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.gcode-ls/flavors/
User flavor directory.
.TP
.I ~/.gcode-ls/flavors/prusa.gcode-flavor.toml
The embedded Prusa flavor copied for user access on startup.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The server exited successfully.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred while starting or running the server.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR language-server-protocol (7)
